Z||000000||mshill||01-17-2001||04:22 PM||||Just a headsup for those of you who are doing a 3.4L swap or have one and are considering the underdrive pulley from the FieroStore.  The alternator/water pump drive belt that they include with the pulley is too small.  The alternator has the heat shield hitting the block and the belt is still about 1 inch too short.  I will post a new belt part number when I find it at autozone.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-17-2001||05:31 PM||||That’s funny, I have the under drive pulley on my 2.8-liter engine and the belt that they supplied was fine. The 3.4-liter engine accepts the accessories from the 2.8-liter engine so they should be exactly the same right?||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||01-17-2001||05:52 PM||||That's what I had suspected.  Is it possible that they sent me the wrong belt?  In the underdrive pulley kit I did get only two bolts that were both at least 1/2 inch too long for the Fiero.  Wrong kit maybe?<P>BTW, do you know the belt part number you received with your pulley?  I can check to see if I was sent the wrong one.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||01-17-2001||09:13 PM||||OK,  I forced it on and tighted it and have about 1/4 inch clearance between the heat shield and the block.  So all is well.<BR>||||reg||1
